  "description": {
    "text": "Ten English e-Cards shown at the Pokémon Center in New York in August 2002, to demonstrate the Nintendo e-Reader's dot codes before the device and the Expedition set came out in the United States. They are near-final versions of Expedition cards, translated and printed by Media Factory in Japan rather than by Wizards of the Coast: they have Japanese backs, \"Sample\" in the bottom right corner, card numbers out of 093 and e-Reader IDs beginning with M (M-16-# on Pikachu), and their text and some attacks differ from Expedition's.\n\nThey were never handed out to the public, but some reached collectors.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "title": "WikiDex: New York Press Conference 2002 (TCG)",
        "url": "https://www.wikidex.net/wiki/New_York_Press_Conference_2002_(TCG)"
      },
      {
        "title": "Elite Fourum: Sample ereader cards with Japanese back",
        "url": "https://www.elitefourum.com/t/sample-ereader-cards-with-japanese-back/24877"
      },
      {
        "title": "Elite Fourum: E reader sample set",
        "url": "https://www.elitefourum.com/t/e-reader-sample-set/10069"
      }
    ]
  },
  "tell": {
    "text": "A \"Sample\" overprint, and a number out of 093",
    "sources": [
      {
        "title": "WikiDex: New York Press Conference 2002 (TCG)",
        "url": "https://www.wikidex.net/wiki/New_York_Press_Conference_2002_(TCG)"
      },
      {
        "title": "Elite Fourum: Sample ereader cards with Japanese back",
        "url": "https://www.elitefourum.com/t/sample-ereader-cards-with-japanese-back/24877"
      }
    ]
  },
